Part 2 — EFM Testing & Recovery Scenarios (15 Minutes)


---

1. Why EFM

VCS/SAN vs EFM

VCS/SAN	EFM

Infrastructure-focused failover	Database-aware failover
Storage-centric	PostgreSQL-centric
Handles node/storage failure	Understands DB state
Limited corruption awareness	Better database recovery awareness


Objective

Improve database-level failover and recovery orchestration.


---

2. EFM Testing Scenarios Performed

Scenario 1 — Primary Database Failure

Tested

Automatic standby promotion

Failover handling

Service continuity

Recovery timing


Outcome

Validated automatic failover capability and recovery readiness.


---

Scenario 2 — Network Isolation Scenario

Tested

Cluster communication handling

Witness functionality

Split-brain prevention


Outcome

Validated cluster protection and failover decision capability.


---

Scenario 3 — PITR & WAL Recovery Validation

Tested

Archived WAL recovery

PITR validation

Recovery consistency validation


Outcome

Validated recoverability objectives during recovery scenarios.


---

Scenario 4 — Corruption Recovery Readiness

Tested

Backup restore procedures

PITR recovery process

Recovery operational procedures

Recovery validation checks


Outcome

Validated preparedness for logical and physical corruption scenarios.


---

3. Key Learnings

Learning	Benefit

Recovery must be validated	Improved recovery confidence
Corruption may propagate through replication	Detection controls are critical
Failover alone is not sufficient	PITR capability remains essential
Operational procedures are important	Faster recovery response



---

4. Final Conclusion

Final Message

The initiative improved overall database resiliency, recoverability, corruption detection capability, and operational readiness across both VCS/SAN and EFM-based environments.


